# What a step makes inside and hands back stands inside its frame: `tidy` hands back what `strip` made in it.
# The memory made and used inside a step lives inside its frame; the own arrow of an opened step is a point on its
# border that keeps what the body gives back, at the step's moment, and a value its call is handed crosses the frame to
# the step inside that takes it (mathematics.md, "One fine plan, every picture its image").

route clean.run
step run/load
step run/load/Table()
step run/tidy
step run/tidy/strip
step run/tidy/strip/Table()
step run/show

line entry > run call
line run/load/Table() > Table@run/load/Table() value
line Table@run/load/Table() > run/load value                        # load hands back what its body made
line run/load > Table·t@run/load value
line Table·t@run/load > run/tidy/strip/Table() value                # tidy's t, and strip's, is read by Table() in strip
line run/tidy/strip/Table() > Table@run/tidy/strip/Table() value
line Table@run/tidy/strip/Table() > run/tidy/strip value            # strip hands back what its body made
line run/tidy/strip > Table·t@run/tidy/strip value
line Table·t@run/tidy/strip > run/tidy value                        # tidy hands back what strip made in it
line run/tidy > Table·t@run/tidy value
line Table·t@run/tidy > run/show value
line run/show > Screen own

home Table@run/load/Table() run/load
home Table·t@run/load run
home Table@run/tidy/strip/Table() run/tidy/strip
home Table·t@run/tidy/strip run/tidy
home Table·t@run/tidy run

side entry left
side Screen right
